<section class="weekly-section weekly-section--lead">
<div class="container">
<div class="weekly-secnum">Opening finding</div>
<h2>An agent payment client signed the amount the seller chose</h2>
<p class="weekly-lead-p">V12's 22 October disclosure describes x402 payment clients, used by AI agents to pay per API call, passing a server's amount, recipient and token straight to the signing code. The default setup applied no spending limit. A hostile server could obtain a signed authorization for a wallet's full token balance "without a separate approval prompt".<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></p>
<p>Holding the key let the client pay. It did not establish authority for the amount a counterparty named.</p>
<div class="weekly-limit"><span class="weekly-limit-label">Evidence limits</span>V12 tested locally, submitted no live transaction and reports the critical findings fixed by 20 August. No exploitation, loss or CVE is reported. Mastercard's new agent payment service builds on x402; no reviewed source shows it was affected.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a>, <a href="#s3">3</a></sup></div>
<div class="weekly-figure"><div class="weekly-figcaption-label">Explanatory / Reported signing path, default client setup</div><div class="weekly-flow weekly-flow--3"><div class="weekly-flow-step"><span class="weekly-flow-num">01 / Server response</span><b>402 Payment Required</b><span>Server sets amount, token, recipient and network.</span></div><div class="weekly-flow-step"><span class="weekly-flow-num">02 / Client default</span><b>First option selected</b><span>No per-payment limit or total budget applied.</span></div><div class="weekly-flow-step weekly-flow-step--outcome"><span class="weekly-flow-num">03 / Result</span><b>Signed authorization</b><span>Could cover the wallet's full token balance.</span></div></div><div class="weekly-limit">A valid signature shows the wallet signed. It does not show anyone approved that amount for that recipient.</div><p class="weekly-figcaption">Explanatory diagram by Jochanni Labs, based on <a href="https://v12.sh/blog/x402" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">V12's disclosure of 22 October 2026</a>. Simplified; not a screenshot or a view of private systems.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="weekly-section">
<div class="container">
<div class="weekly-secnum">01 / Market Response</div>
